From 4b1b6025b18a9ff96dd5ed3542ada5f27fd0c7b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jean-Michel Hautbois <jeanmichel.hautbois@yoseli.org>
Date: Wed, 8 Apr 2026 12:17:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] m68k: add bits/atomic.h using sys_atomic_cmpxchg_32

uClibc-ng ships no m68k-specific bits/atomic.h, so the build falls
back to the generic include/bits/atomic.h which is explicitly
non-atomic: its atomic_compare_and_exchange_val_acq is a three-step
read/compare/write sequence documented as "no support for atomic
operations" by its author.

On a single-core Coldfire under kernel preemption, two userspace
threads can race inside that sequence and both believe their CAS
succeeded. When the race hits an NPTL pthread mutex __lll_lock /
__lll_unlock pair, the futex word ends up inconsistent and one
thread deadlocks in __lll_lock_wait while the lock byte is 0 and
nobody holds it. Observed reproducibly on mcf5441x under sustained
rsyslog load.

Provide a real m68k bits/atomic.h that uses the existing
sys_atomic_cmpxchg_32 syscall. The kernel runs the compare-and-swap
under mmap_read_lock on a uniprocessor non-preempt kernel, which is
atomic with respect to other userspace threads of the same process.

Defining only __arch_compare_and_exchange_val_32_acq is enough:
include/atomic.h derives the bool flavour, exchange via CAS loop and
the fetch primitives from this single 32-bit CAS.

Upstream: not-submitted, m68k atomic operations via sys_atomic_cmpxchg_32
Signed-off-by: Jean-Michel Hautbois <jeanmichel.hautbois@yoseli.org>
---
 libc/sysdeps/linux/m68k/bits/atomic.h | 96 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 96 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libc/sysdeps/linux/m68k/bits/atomic.h

diff --git a/libc/sysdeps/linux/m68k/bits/atomic.h b/libc/sysdeps/linux/m68k/bits/atomic.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..ebdb00909
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libc/sysdeps/linux/m68k/bits/atomic.h
@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+/* Atomic operations for m68k Coldfire / Linux.
+   Copyright (C) 2026 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
